{
  "record": "RRP002_DEV_V2_FLOOR_CORRECTION",
  "schema": 1,
  "supersedes": "RRP002_DEV_V2_FLOOR.json, whose `leak_check` assertion is FALSE and whose shortcut floor omitted the strongest honest predictor",
  "what_was_wrong": {
    "the_false_assertion": "RRP002_DEV_V2_FLOOR.json records that every row was 'asserted to contain neither its reference_text nor its id in the model-visible prompt'. For the 144 unanswerable rows that is false: the complete gold object is printed in the prompt's own rule text.",
    "why_the_check_missed_it": "instrument.py compared the needle against json.dumps(prompt), which escapes the inner quotes, so a needle of {\"status\":\"UNKNOWN\"} could never match a haystack of {\\\"status\\\":\\\"UNKNOWN\\\"}.",
    "measured_leaks_raw_text": 144,
    "measured_leaks_caught_by_the_json_dumps_check": 0,
    "unanswerable_rows": 144,
    "is_the_bank_broken": "No. Forge v2 states the abstention contract in its rule text by design -- it is telling the model what to return. The bank is sound; the ERROR was asserting the absence of something present and then pricing the floor as if it were absent."
  },
  "the_missing_predictor": {
    "name": "copy_prompt_sentinel",
    "definition": "emit the single {\"status\":\"X\"} literal printed in this row's own prompt; if none is printed, emit {\"value\":0}",
    "answer_agnostic": true,
    "reads": "the model-visible prompt only",
    "why_it_must_be_in_the_floor": "it is the direct v2 analogue of v1's copy_question_sentinel, which CL-022 already obliged the programme to compare abstention against. v2 simply never had one.",
    "prompt_structure_measured": "288 of 336 prompts print exactly one status literal and 48 print none; for all 144 unanswerable rows the printed literal IS the gold. The two families that print none (ledger_replay, register_machine) contribute zero unanswerable rows."
  },
